# RME billing correction — financial integrity foundation (rule 188)

Full evidence: `docs/AUDIT-RME-BILLING-CORRECTION-PAYMENT-REFUND-FOUNDATION-1.md` (every claim cites file:line).

> **Forward reference (2026-10-17):** `FEATURE-RME-INVOICE-CORRECTION-RECEIPT-FOUNDATION-1` (rule 190) shipped a
> PRE-PAYMENT correction workflow behind the default-OFF flag `rme.invoice_correction`. Lines below that say no
> correction table/route/permission exists, or that invoices are immutable by ABSENCE of a mutation path, describe the
> state before that release; while the flag is off they remain behaviourally true. Rule 190 is authoritative for what
> now exists.

**This rule activates nothing.** No correction, refund, Rp0 adjustment, permission, route or table exists for it.
`FEATURE-RME-BILLING-CORRECTION-PAYMENT-ADJUSTMENT-1` is not started. An audit GO is never a feature GO — never report
billing correction as active until its own implementation has shipped, deployed and been verified.

Labels: **CURRENT** (verified), **APPROVED_SCOPE** (owner-requested, not built), **PROPOSED** (design only — must
never be cited as production behaviour), **PENDING_OWNER_DECISION** (see audit §26, D1–D23).

## 1. Billing source of truth — CURRENT
- RME billing = `trx_rme_invoices`, `trx_rme_invoice_items`, `trx_rme_payments` (module `app/Modules/RmeInvoice`).
- Lab billing (`trx_invoices`, `trx_payments`, `app/Modules/Invoice`) is a **separate domain**. Never mix them; a
  correction to one never touches the other (rule 186 #18).
- `invoice_number` and `payment_number` are DB-unique. "No. Kwitansi" printed = `payment_number` of the newest payment.

## 2. Invoice lifecycle — CURRENT
- Statuses `DRAFT/UNPAID/PARTIAL/PAID/VOID` exist as constants, but **creation writes `UNPAID` directly** and **no
  application path writes `DRAFT` or `VOID`** (they are only read/filtered). Do not assume either is reachable.
- Totals are committed inside `RmeInvoiceService::create()`; afterwards only `status` is rewritten, derived from
  `SUM(payments.amount)`. There is no edit, delete or void endpoint. Invoices are immutable by ABSENCE of a mutation
  path, not by a designed control.
- `RmeInvoice::recalculateTotals()` double-subtracts discount and is unused — never call it from new code without fixing it.

## 3. Payment lifecycle — CURRENT
- Payments are append-only de facto: `RmePaymentRepository` has only `create/forInvoice/latestPaymentNumberForMonth`.
  Every payment path locks the invoice row (`lockForUpdate`) and caps `amount` at the remaining balance.
- `paid_at` is client-supplied and decides the revenue period. **[UPDATED by rule 189 §5]** it is now refused when in
  the future (`> now + 60 s`, all three payment paths); backdating is still unbounded (D24), so it is still never a
  trustworthy authority for new financial logic.
- Any payment > 0 (full or partial) completes a `cashier_pending` visit; the balance stays receivable.
- **Payments must never be updated, re-amounted, re-batched, re-branched or soft-deleted to effect a correction.** The
  schema permits soft delete and `paidAmount()` excludes soft-deleted rows — so a soft delete silently rewrites balances
  and revenue. Corrections go through their own records. **[UPDATED by rule 189 §6]** the `RmePayment` model now refuses
  update (except `patient_id`) and soft/force delete at the application layer; raw SQL is still not stopped.

## 4. Carry-over and payment batches — CURRENT
- `payment_batch_uuid` is minted once per cashier action only by the control/visit allocation paths; plain `pay()`
  writes NULL. Oversight counts `COALESCE(uuid, 'payment:'||id)` per INVOICE branch.
- A batch may span several invoices and branches (`payment.branch_id` = invoice branch).
- PROPOSED invariant: a correction targets exactly ONE invoice; it never edits another invoice's payments, never moves an
  allocation between invoices, never changes `payment_batch_uuid`.

## 5. Receipt behaviour — CURRENT
- Receipts (`rme.cashier.receipt.show/.pdf`) are rendered live from current rows on every request, PAID invoices only.
  No snapshot, version, superseded status, stored PDF or print/view audit exists.
- Consequence: once corrections exist, reprinting a pre-correction receipt would silently show corrected values.
- PROPOSED: the correction record stores an immutable original-document snapshot; the original receipt renders from it
  marked superseded, the live receipt is marked revised with the correction reference. No receipt-version table unless
  a later audit proves the snapshot insufficient.

## 6. Refund capability — CURRENT: none
> **Forward reference (2026-10-31):** the refund REQUEST and its approval now exist (rule 215, flag
> `rme.billing_refund_request` OFF, identity allowlist EMPTY). They decide, never pay: refund SETTLEMENT still
> does not exist, and the invariant below still holds.
- No refund table, status, permission, route, service or report exists.
- `config/rme_invoice.php` `refund_terms` is owner-approved PRINTED text (Kawat Gigi ≤ 2×24 jam; payout at month end)
  that the system does not implement. Never treat printed terms as system behaviour.
- PROPOSED invariant: refund approval ≠ money returned. Only a recorded settlement reduces cash. Refund amount is derived
  server-side from the ledger, never from input.

## 7. Approval capability — CURRENT
- RME billing has **no approval workflow**. The codebase has no generic approval engine; approvals are domain-specific
  (PatientMergeCase, DoctorBranchLock/Cover, BranchChangeRequest, LegacyRme publish, SATUSEHAT change control).
- `Gate::before` grants Super Admin every ability before any policy runs, so maker≠checker MUST be enforced inside the
  service transaction under the row lock (PatientMergeCase pattern), never only in a policy.

## 8. Audit requirements — CURRENT
- **[SUPERSEDED by rule 189 §3]** invoice creation (`RME_INVOICE_CREATED`) and payment recording
  (`RME_PAYMENT_RECORDED`) are now audited, PII-free, inside the fact's transaction. Before Phase 0 the module wrote
  nothing to `sys_audit_logs` (BCF-02).
- `sys_audit_logs` has `old_values/new_values` jsonb, `performed_by`, `performed_at`, no `updated_at`; append-only by
  convention, not DB-enforced.
- PROPOSED: every correction/refund/receipt-supersession event is audited with ids, amounts and statuses only — no patient
  name, KTP/NIK or clinical text in the payload.

## 9. Financial immutability — invariants for any future work
- Never overwrite an original payment. Never delete or hard-edit historical financial rows.
- Never represent an overpayment as a negative receivable (it would corrupt oversight receivable sums and aging).
- `remainingAmount()` clamps at 0 and therefore hides overpayment (BCF-04): a correction that lowers `grand_total` below
  the paid total must surface an explicit overpayment/refund obligation, never silently report PAID.
- Status is always re-derived from the ledger inside the locking transaction.

## 10. Correction safety invariants — PROPOSED
- One active (submitted/approved) correction per invoice (partial unique index).
- Original snapshot captured at submission; approval re-verifies under lock that the invoice still matches (else STALE).
- Approval never mutates data; application is atomic and idempotent (re-applying is a no-op).
- Lock order: invoice row first, then correction row — the same row every payment path locks.
- Whether a pending correction blocks payment is D10 (recommended: yes).

## 11. Maker–checker separation — PROPOSED
- The maker can never approve their own request, including a Super Admin; the checker needs an explicit permission.
- Rejection requires a reason. Approval and financial settlement use separate permissions (D18).
- Front Office = Admin Klinik + Kasir permissions, so separation must be per ACCOUNT. Measure per-branch staffing before
  arming (an enforced but unstaffable control is a stop-the-line finding).

## 12. Rp0 eligibility — APPROVED_SCOPE + PROPOSED
- APPROVED_SCOPE: Rp0 adjustment only for **KONTROL** or **KONSULTASI DOKTER**.
- CURRENT sources of truth: Kontrol = server-derived `visit_type` from a validated `follow_up_of_visit_id`
  (`StoreClinicVisitRequest`, rule 185 #17-#21); Konsultasi = treatment `TRT-CONS` / category code `consultation` (data
  only — no flag column).
- CURRENT defect: the cashier types `unit_price`/`discount` freely (tariffs never read; discount uncapped) — an Rp0 or
  negative line needs no approval today (BCF-01). Any Rp0 approval workflow is bypassable until this is closed.
  **[REFRAMED by rule 194 (D21 revised 2026-10-20): the cashier-typed price IS the owner-approved policy; a negative
  line/total is now refused (discount ≤ line gross). Still open: original-invoice Rp0 (D21g/D22) and the discount
  policy (D21c).]**
- PROPOSED: Rp0 per ITEM (D11); eligibility from `treatment_id` + category, never from `description` or client
  `visit_type`; unrelated treatments and carried-over receivables are never zeroed; an Rp0 outcome never fabricates a
  Rp0 payment row (D22).
- CURRENT: an Rp0 invoice can never become PAID and stays UNPAID forever (production invoice #36); it is counted as
  "unpaid" by the Owner/RME dashboards (BCF-05).

## 13. Cross-branch financial authorization — CURRENT
- Cashier/policy scope = `RmeWorkingBranchScope` (context-bound roles pinned to their working branch; non-context roles
  fall through to every RME branch — F-01).
- Oversight scope = `ClinicOversightScope` (active, RME-enabled, not MAIN; requested `branch_id` only narrows; out of
  scope = 404). Any correction oversight surface MUST use `ClinicOversightScope`, never `RmeWorkingBranchScope`.
- A correction and its refund belong to the corrected invoice's branch.

## 14. Finance Klinik / Data Analyst scope — CURRENT + APPROVED_SCOPE
- CURRENT: exactly the four oversight permissions (rule 186); no `manage_rme_billing`, no write permission.
- APPROVED_SCOPE: sidebar group **BILLING CORRECTION** (Daftar Pasien Koreksi; Riwayat & Detail Koreksi) for both roles,
  identical initial access, independently assignable permissions; read/print/PDF/export only.
- PROPOSED: new `view_billing_correction_oversight` + existing `export_oversight_data`; GET-only routes under
  `/oversight/billing-corrections`. That implementation sprint must amend rule 186's "exactly four" statement. Never grant
  `manage_rme_billing` to make oversight data visible.

## 15. Oversight dashboard preservation — CURRENT
- Rule 186/187 KPI formulas stay unchanged: patients, transactions (batch identity), revenue
  (`SUM(trx_rme_payments.amount)` by `paid_at`, invoice branch, never `grand_total`), current receivables, cancellations
  by `cancelled_at`. Corrections must not change patient or cancellation counts.

## 16. Reporting reconciliation — PROPOSED, PENDING_OWNER_DECISION (D8/D9)
- Recommended Model C: gross collections unchanged, refunds reported separately by settlement date, net = gross − settled
  refunds, per invoice branch. Never restate a closed period silently.
- Doctor performance reads `grand_total` and item `subtotal`; corrections must be reflected and traceable there.

