## 19. Implementation prerequisites
- Phase 0 before any correction work: financial audit log (BCF-02 — **done**), server price authority + discount cap
  (BCF-01, D21 — **price authority closed by rule 194 (manual pricing); discount cap D21c open**), bounded `paid_at` (BCF-03 — future bound **done**, backdating D24 open), invoice-per-visit
  race guard (BCF-08 — **done**). See rule 189.
- Receipt snapshot (Phase E) before post-payment correction (Phase C). Refund (Phase D) only after D4–D6, D18.
- Additive migrations only (`migrate --force`), never `migrate:fresh`/`db:wipe`; payments table untouched.

## 20. Regression requirements
- Lock/constraint/concurrency tests run on PostgreSQL 16 (SQLite compiles `lockForUpdate` to nothing and does not abort
  the transaction on error).
- Existing suites stay green: CashierBilling, RmePayment, PatientOutstandingReceivableCarryOver,
  RmeDoctorCashierCompletionGate, RmeControlVisitReceivableCarryOverPayment, RmeReceiptOnePage, RmeReportTodayDefault,
  ClinicOversight/*.
- The 50-case matrix in audit §22 is the minimum for the feature.
